hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15462","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Uthman ibn Talhah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House and prayed two rakahs facing you when you enter, between the two pillars."
"15463","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah ibn Jawshan, from Uqbah ibn Aws, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached on the day of the conquest of Makkah, so he said: There is no god but Allah alone, He helped His servant and defeated the confederates alone. Hushaym said another time: Praise be to Allah who kept His promise and helped His servant. Indeed every distinction that was in the Jahiliyyah, counted and claimed, and every blood or claim, is placed under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the House and the watering of the pilgrims. Indeed the victim of mistaken intentional killing, Hushaym said once: with the whip and the stick and the stone, has an aggravated blood money: one hundred camels, forty of them pregnant with their young in their bellies. And he said once: Forty from a thaniyah to a bazil of its year, all of them khalifah."
"15464","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, that he said in this hadith: And indeed the victim of mistaken intentional killing with the whip and the stick and the stone is one hundred camels, forty of them pregnant with their young in their bellies. So whoever adds a camel is of the people of the Jahiliyyah."
"15465","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with close to that, except that he said: One hundred camels: thirty hiqqah, and thirty jadhah, and thirty daughters of labun, and forty thaniyah khalifah to a bazil of its year."
